---
import SiteFrame from "../layouts/SiteFrame.astro";
const updated = "August 30, 2026";
---
<SiteFrame title="Privacy — Blaine County Preparedness"
           description="What we collect, why, and what we don't do with it.">
  <article class="doc">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="h1">What we keep, and what we don't</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <p class="lede">
      Blaine County Preparedness is a small community site. We collect the
      least we can get away with, we don't sell anything to anyone, and you
      can ask us to delete your information at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      If you only read the site, we collect nothing about you. No account,
      no tracking, no advertising profiles.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you sign in to take part in The Table, you sign in through Google.
      We never see or store your password — Google handles that. What we
      receive and store is:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your display name, as Google provides it</li>
      <li>Your email address</li>
      <li>Your profile picture, if you have one</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We also store what you write: your threads and replies, and when you
      posted them. That's the point of a forum.
    </p>

    <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
    <p>
      Your name appears next to what you write, so conversations have people
      in them rather than anonymous voices. Your email lets us reach you
      about your account or something you posted, and lets us tell one
      person from another. That's all it's for.
    </p>

    <h2>What we don't do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We don't sell your information. Not to anyone, ever.</li>
      <li>We don't run advertising or advertising trackers.</li>
      <li>We don't share your email with other users.</li>
      <li>We don't email you things you didn't ask for.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who can see what</h2>
    <p>
      Anyone can read the forum. Your display name and anything you post are
      public. Your email address is not shown to other users — only site
      administrators can see it.
    </p>

    <h2>Where it lives</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted by Cloudflare. Accounts and forum content are stored
      with Supabase. Both are established providers with their own security
      practices. Sign-in is handled by Google.
    </p>

    <h2>Deleting your information</h2>
    <p>
      Write to us and we'll delete your account and, if you want, your posts.
      No process, no argument. Deleting your account removes your name, email,
      and picture from our records.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      This site isn't intended for children under 13, and we don't knowingly
      collect information from them.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes in a way that matters, we'll say so on the site
      rather than quietly editing the page.
    </p>

    <h2>Getting in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about any of this, or a request to delete your information:
      <a href="mailto:contacts@bcp.zone">contacts@bcp.zone</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</SiteFrame>

<style>
  .doc { max-width: 66ch; margin: 0 auto; }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--sage); margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .h1 {
    font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6vw, 3.2rem); line-height: 1.05;
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem; color: var(--snowmelt);
  }
  .updated {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--sage); opacity: 0.7;
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
  }
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--body); font-style: italic; font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.6; color: var(--sage); margin: 0 0 2.4rem;
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 400; font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--snowmelt); margin: 2.2rem 0 0.7rem;
  }
  p, li {
    font-family: var(--body); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--snowmelt);
  }
  p { margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
  ul { margin: 0 0 1.2rem; padding-left: 1.4rem; }
  li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  a { color: var(--oxide); text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
